*.yuv
# Raw test sequences (y4m) are huge and reproducible from their source URLs
# (e.g. src/samples/aomctc_test_set/a1_4k_source.txt). Never commit them.
*.y4m
*.crdownload
__pycache__/
*.pyc
opsnr.stt

# ML artifacts. The models tree IS versioned: the student checkpoints, gate CSVs,
# oracle simulations, metrics and exported C headers are what the thesis cites, and
# they are small -- the whole tree minus the two exclusions below is ~1.9 MB.
# The `!` lines must come BEFORE the exclusions: the LAST matching pattern wins.
*.npz
*.pt
!results/models/**/*.npz
!results/models/**/*.pt
# Exclusion 1 -- a hash-named training cache (~334 MB), regenerable by rerunning
# build_regret_targets.py. Excluded as a DIRECTORY, so nothing inside can be
# re-included; that is intended here.
results/models/_cache_regret/
# Exclusion 2 -- the two ConvNeXt surrogates, 112.6 MB EACH. GitHub hard-rejects
# any file above 100 MB, so committing these does not merely bloat the repo, it
# makes `git push` fail. They belong in the Zenodo deposit alongside the dataset,
# not in git. Everything else under surrogate_*/ (metrics.csv, config, curves) is
# versioned.
results/models/surrogate_real/surrogate_best.pt
results/models/surrogate_regret/surrogate_regret_best.pt
.venv-ml/

# Dataset payloads are huge (dataset_h9 ~31 GB of .pkl) and reproducible from the
# instrumented encoder + scripts + source YUV. Never commit them to git.
# Only manifests / metadata are tracked.
results/dataset/*.bin
results/dataset/*.pkl
results/dataset/blocks/
# Note: the pattern must exclude the *contents* (trailing /*), not the directory
# itself -- git never descends into an excluded directory, so a `!` negation
# under `results/dataset_h9/` would be unreachable.
results/dataset_h9/*
results/dataset_new/
# ...except the small derived metadata: the provenance ledger and the label
# histogram (~145 KB total) are the reproducibility record of the dataset.
!results/dataset_h9/manifest.csv
!results/dataset_h9/label_histogram.csv
!results/dataset_h9/label_distribution.md
# h8_probs (4 MB), gnn_probs (6 MB) e partstats (110 MB) sao versionados: dumps de
# analise que sustentam o teto H8, o replay do Approach B e o RESULTADOS_C1.
#
# Os fluxos de bits (.ivf/.obu, 1151 arquivos / 1,18 GB, maior deles 8,6 MB) tambem
# sao versionados, por decisao explicita -- inclusive os que vivem nos diretorios
# _work, onde estao 758 dos 1151. Ressalva registrada e mantida: eles sao saida
# DETERMINISTICA do codificador, e os YUV de origem continuam fora do repositorio,
# de modo que sua presenca nao permite verificar nada que os CSV ja versionados nao
# permitam. Nenhum deles chega perto do limite de 100 MB por arquivo, e nenhum usa
# LFS.

# Transient build/training logs. The per-campaign run.log / .done files ARE kept:
# they carry each encode's time/PSNR/kbps and are the provenance of the tables.
logs/
# PID files of detached campaigns -- meaningless once the run ends.
*.pid
